\section{Choose a prediction route}{
Two terms recur below. \emph{Conditional} uncertainty treats the estimated kernel
scales (sigma) and shapes as known and carries only the uncertainty in the
regression coefficients (and an estimated dispersion, where the model has
one). \emph{Joint} uncertainty lets the kernel parameters and the coefficients
vary together.\tabular{lllll}{
